tasks.notes:
Contents of this part.
- Tool exposure: getActiveToolNames, getCallableToolNames, _getToolExposure (direct, model-only, codemode, deferred, hidden), and allowed/excluded tool filters.
- _applyToolLoadout runs prepareLoadout hooks.
- _rebuildSystemPrompt and _preparePromptAndToolLoadout use buildSystemPrompt and section diffs. Prompt snippets and guidelines are normalized.
- Hidden-declarations and forced-system-prompt projections run in transformContext.
- prompt():
  - rejects while compacting or streaming according to the streamingBehavior option;
  - input handlers may consume the input;
  - extension slash-command dispatch;
  - skill command expansion: `<skill name=".." location="..">\nReferences are relative to <baseDir>.\n\n<body>\n</skill>` with the frontmatter stripped;
  - prompt template expansion;
  - images processed through processImage under the model's input limits;
  - before_agent_start;
  - pending bash and custom messages flushed;
  - _runAgentPrompt and _handlePostAgentRun (retry, overflow recovery, before_settle).
- Queues:
  - steer/followUp follow the one-at-a-time vs all modes.
  - Extension-origin queued slash commands are treated as raw text (#2023).
  - clearQueue, pendingMessageCount.
- setModel/cycleModel: persist to the session, optionally persist defaults, per-model thinking overrides, scoped model order.
- setThinkingLevel/cycleThinkingLevel: clamp via clampThinkingLevel/getSupportedThinkingLevels.
- Steering and follow-up modes are synced from settings.

The concurrency guard is tested by agent-session-concurrent: a second prompt() while streaming throws unless streamingBehavior is set. waitForIdle and abort semantics need careful async ordering (promise resolvers become oneshot channels or condvars).

All become native examples. They depend on the native pi-tui Component/Overlay API and on ui.custom/setEditorComponent/setHeader/setFooter.

What each exercises:
- overlay-qa-tests (1450 lines) is the manual QA harness for:
  - overlay anchors, margins, percent sizing, maxHeight;
  - visible callbacks, onHandle setHidden;
  - nonCapturing overlays;
  - focus, unfocus, hide;
  - streaming bash output with OSC 8 links;
  - hslToRgb.
  Port it last, after the TUI overlay API stabilizes. It doubles as an interactive test for tmux-based QA.
- rainbow-editor subclasses CustomEditor with a 60 ms animation and /ultrathink/gi highlighting. Natively, use composition: wrap the default editor and override render.
- modal-editor: vim-like modes.
- Key handling must go through configurable keybindings, never hardcoded key checks.
